        "original_id": "a9ee4532-952d-5083-b47f-e3af72044d73",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steve Sekely, King Baggot, Roland Varno, Gail Patrick, Nancy Kelly\n- Works: Women in Bondage, The Return of the Vampire, My Name Is Julia Ross, Gunga Din, Three Faces West, Three's a Crowd, Flight to Nowhere, Scared to Death\n- Concepts: stage names, publicity titles, immigration status\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Sekely was born as Székely István.\n- Steve Sekely was also known by several names tied to his professional and immigration status, including Stefan Szekely.\n- King Baggot was the first individually publicized leading man in America.\n- King Baggot was referred to as \"King of the Movies,\" \"The Most Photographed Man in the World,\" and \"The Man Whose Face Is As Familiar As The Man In The Moon.\"\n- Women in Bondage was directed by Steve Sekely and starred Gail Patrick and Nancy Kelly.\n- In the 1930s and 1940s, Roland Varno appeared in dozens of films, including The Return of the Vampire, My Name Is Julia Ross, Gunga Din, Three Faces West, Women in Bondage, Three's a Crowd, Flight to Nowhere, and Scared to Death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
